# Swingshot anywhere's row (More controls' first, 0.1.13): the way to VR Options as bodypage.sim goes, by the sticks with
# the right controller off, eleven rows down to VR Controls; there eleven down to its last row, More controls, and A
# opens it. Its first row stepped once: Swingshot anywhere On. Two down (past Ledge shimmy), Hide black bars stepped
# right then left: "[vr-view] Hide black bars: off, the game's own", then "on". Two down (past Menu pointer),
# Arm moves stepped: Buttons ("[vr-controls] Arm moves: Buttons"); five down, the page's last, Sparkles on the bolts
# stepped: Off. B back to VR Controls. The [vr-swing] line says "Swingshot anywhere: on", the [vr-rig] lines arm moves
# buttons, then sparkles_in_world off, and no line says a page has more rows than the port's 12; the run's
# vr-options.txt keeps swing_anywhere 1, hide_bars 1 and button_moves 1. (0.1.12's VR Controls had 16 rows, and the port
# shows 12 of a page: its last four could not be reached. 0.1.13's first try of this sim stopped at row 11 for that.)
